sha,\nbathe Lord Vishnu with Panchamrut (milk, buttermilk, ghee, sugar, and honey). Worship is the greatest, without wealth and deceit. Charun Nirupya Payasi Shipivishtaya Vishnave. 51. Sukteen ten purusham yajet sushamahithah.\nOffer the Naivedyam (food offering) which is of the highest quality, so that it may satisfy the person. 52. Meaning of the word\n\nPuja—worship; Cha—also; Mahatim—extremely flashy; Kuryat—does; Vitta-shatya—the attitude of stinginess;\nVivarjitah—abandoning; Charum—food offered in Yagya; Nirupya—looking properly; Payasi—with milk; Shipivishitaya—\nTo the Supreme Being residing in the heart of every living being; Vishnave—to Vishnu; Sukteena—by the Vedic mantra chanting named Purusha-sukta; Tena—by that\nPurusham—of the Lord; Yajet—worship; Su-samahitah—with concentration; Naivedyam—food offered to the deity;"
